## Phase 5: API Cost Optimization Suite

**Objective:** Minimize runtime financial cost. Ensure that Socratic study sessions processing thousands of tokens cost fractions of a cent, and heavy note re-indexing never duplicates API charges.

---

### 5A. Gemini Explicit Context Caching (Session Caching)

**Problem:** In Socratic view sessions, every time the user answers a question, Deep-Notes sends the entire active note context + RAG chunks + system instructions to the LLM. In a 10-question session on a long note, this processes 10,000 to 20,000 identical prefix tokens repeatedly, multiplying costs.

**Fix:** Create a temporary Gemini **Explicit Context Cache** for the active note on first generation. Subsequent evaluation calls and follow-ups reference this `cachedContent` identifier, **saving 90% on input token costs**.

**Code Blueprint — `src/ai.ts`:**
```typescript
interface GeminiCacheObject {
    name: string; // Cache resource identifier
    expireTime: string;
}

export class GeminiCacheManager {
    private activeCache: { filePath: string; cacheName: string; expiresAt: number } | null = null;

    async getOrCreateCache(
        filePath: string,
        noteContent: string,
        systemPrompt: string,
        apiKey: string
    ): Promise<string> {
        const now = Date.now();
        if (this.activeCache && this.activeCache.filePath === filePath && this.activeCache.expiresAt > now) {
            return this.activeCache.cacheName;
        }

        // Cache must expire to prevent storage leaks (TTL of 15 minutes is perfect for a study session)
        const ttlMinutes = 15;
        const expireTime = new Date(now + ttlMinutes * 60000).toISOString();

        const url = `https://generativelanguage.googleapis.com/v1beta/cachedContents?key=${apiKey}`;
        const response = await requestUrl({
            url,
            method: "POST",
            headers: { "Content-Type": "application/json" },
            body: JSON.stringify({
                model: "models/gemini-2.5-flash",
                ttl: `${ttlMinutes * 60}s`,
                contents: [{ role: "user", parts: [{ text: noteContent }] }],
                systemInstruction: { parts: [{ text: systemPrompt }] }
            })
        });

        if (response.status !== 200) {
            throw new Error(`Context caching failed: ${response.text}`);
        }

        const data = response.json as GeminiCacheObject;
        this.activeCache = {
            filePath,
            cacheName: data.name,
            expiresAt: now + ttlMinutes * 60000
        };

        console.debug(`[DeepNotes] Created explicit Gemini context cache: ${data.name} (TTL: 15m)`);
        return data.name;
    }
}
```

---

### 5B. Paragraph-Level Hash-Based Incremental Indexing

**Problem:** Currently, when a note is edited, `indexer.ts` deletes all existing vectors and re-embeds the entire note text. If a user fixes a typo in a 20-paragraph note, they pay for 20 new API embedding requests.

**Fix:** Split notes into paragraph-level chunks, hash the text of each chunk, and store the hash in metadata. During indexing, compare hashes: **only request embeddings for modified paragraphs**.

**Code Blueprint — `src/vectorStore.ts`:**
```typescript
import { createHash } from "crypto";

export function computeTextHash(text: string): string {
    return createHash("md5").update(text.trim()).digest("hex");
}

// Inside indexNote() in VaultVectorStore:
// Compare chunk hashes to only re-embed modified sections
const currentChunks = chunkNote(content, file.path);
const existingItems = await this.index.listItems();
const fileItems = existingItems.filter(i => (i.metadata as any).filePath === file.path);

const existingHashes = new Map<string, string>(); // chunkIndex -> hash
fileItems.forEach(item => {
    const meta = item.metadata as any;
    existingHashes.set(meta.chunkIndex.toString(), meta.textHash);
});

for (const chunk of currentChunks) {
    const textHash = computeTextHash(chunk.text);
    const prevHash = existingHashes.get(chunk.chunkIndex.toString());

    if (prevHash === textHash) {
        // Unchanged paragraph: keep existing vector, skip API call!
        continue;
    }

    // Changed paragraph: proceed to API embedding call
    const vec = await embedFn(chunk.text);
    // ... insert code ...
}
```

